agonal blocks of G are the pairings on E_0^{p,*}; identifying the differentials with its off-diagonal blocks is the remaining step.'","history":2},{"id":"trap-em-dash","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","notes":"PROPOSED (structural, not applied): the density is a symptom of layering corrections onto the original text in place. Moving the 2026-08-09 correction into authorNotes and rewriting the body under convention D would remove most of them at once.","history":2},{"id":"trap-meta-commentary","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"major","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","notes":"AUTHORNOTES FLAG (AGENTS.md 4d, one-voice Cat. H): the whole opening blockquote plus the retraction are dated status content and belong in authorNotes (kinds 'caveat' and 'refined-framing', date 2026-08-09), with the body rewritten under convention D. Struck-through text should be deleted from the prose, not displayed. This single change would also clear the trap-em-dash fail.","history":2},{"id":"trap-negation-contrast","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","notes":"One is a verbatim repeat: 'Nothing structural is lost, only relocated' here and 'The Frobenius structure itself is not lost, only relocated' in rem:frobenius-gram-matrix-context. Same sentence, same correction, two blocks — worth consolidating into one place both can cite.","history":2},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","notes":"CHECKED, WITH FIVE DEFECTS. VERIFIED CORRECT: the rank arithmetic is exactly right - dim H_n = n!, the surviving quotient is sum over at-most-2-row partitions of dim^2 = Catalan (5, 14, 42 for n = 3,4,5), giving corank 1, 10 = 3^2 + 1^2, 78 = 6^2 + 5^2 + 4^2 + 1^2, and the killed dimensions are exactly those of the 3-or-more-row partitions. tau(sigma_i^2) = hz + 1 and tau(sigma_0 sigma_1 sigma_0) = h z^2 + z both match rem:frobenius-gram-matrix-context. a_K = G_{beta, beta*}/G_{1,1} matches def:frobenius-self-pairing-chirality. DEFECTS: (1) THE CO-CASIMIR IDENTIFICATION DOES NOT COMPUTE. With G^{-1}_{ll} = [n]_q!/(dim_q(l) dim(l)) and D_{ll} = 1/dim_q(l), tr(G^{-1} D) = [n]_q! sum 1/(dim_q^2 dim), not sum 1/dim_q. The missing factor is tau(e_l): the co-Casimir trace is sum_l c_l tau(p_l) with c_l = 1/(dim_q tau(p_l)). Either D must be delta_{ll} tau(e_l)/dim_q, or the sentence 'Summing G^{-1} diagonal times 1/dim_q gives exactly sum 1/dim_q' must go. (2) THE GRAM DEFINITION CONTRADICTS THE DISPLAYED MATRIX: the text says G_{ij} = tau(b_i b_j^{-1}), but the matrix shown has first row (1, z, z, z^2, z^2, z^3), which is tau(b_i b_j). With inverses the entries would involve tau(sigma^{-1}) = z - h = 0.4036, not z = 0.6127. Every sibling block (def:frobenius-dual-h3, prop:frobenius-gram-matrix, rem:frobenius-gram-matrix-context) defines it without the inverse. (3) THE CASIMIR IS NOT THE CO-CASIMIR: item 2 writes C_{dim_q} = sum_{ij} (G^{-1})_{ij} b_i b_j, which is the standard Casimir Omega; thm:frobenius-codim-universal defines C_{dim_q} = sum_l p_l/(dim_q(l) tau(p_l)), and the proof of that theorem explicitly distinguishes the two ('the standard Casimir Omega = sum e_i e^i corresponds to the torus with puncture; C_{dim_q} to the torus with a dim_q-labelled puncture'). (4) l(lambda) COLLISION: 'y_lambda = 0 for every lambda with l(lambda) >= 3' means three or more ROWS here, but this chapter defines l(lambda) = height(lambda) - 1 (proof of thm:frobenius-codim-universal), under which three rows is l = 2. As written the sentence keeps the three-row blocks alive, contradicting the corank numbers in the same block. (5) MALFORMED EXPONENT: 'det G = prod_l tau(e_l)^{\\,\\cdot}' has a raised-dot placeholder where the multiplicity belongs (presumably dim(l)^2). Also kappa is used here for the root-of-unity order while prop:gram-determinant-plancherel-ratio uses it for the Gram-determinant ratio and rem:geom-bridge-status for 3/16.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"fail","severity":"minor","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","notes":"The strongest of these, 'equivalent to computing all pages', would need the differentials to be recoverable from G; the block only says they are 'encoded in the off-diagonal blocks under filtered inversion'.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:r08","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"n/a","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"folio-assistant-sci/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","notes":"block has no .lean sibling","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by"